Fixed :meth:`Component.to_ical <icalendar.cal.component.Component.to_ical>` writing a lone carriage return from an ``UNKNOWN`` value, :class:`~icalendar.prop.unknown.vUnknown`, into the content line, for example after :meth:`Component.from_jcal <icalendar.cal.component.Component.from_jcal>` or :meth:`Component.from_xcal <icalendar.cal.component.Component.from_xcal>`. Parsers that end a line at a lone carriage return read the rest of the value as a new property. Like a line feed, a carriage return in a content line now raises a :exc:`ValueError`. I used AI to assist me with this change. @shamsManna
